This product reproduces short portions of the Deceptive Grounding Benchmark
(https://github.com/CedricCaruzzo/deceptive-grounding-benchmark, commit
61b0281d8d3897f53bef3f7402727c905614c1e4), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0:

  - the text of AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT from its config.py, verbatim;
  - the wording of its query ("What does the literature say about using {X}
    to treat {C}?") from benchmark_runner.py;
  - the layout of its "doc_injection" user message ("Retrieved literature
    documents: ... [Document n — source: <id>] ... Based on the above
    documents, ...") from benchmark_runner.py, re-implemented here and extended
    with this project's answer-format instruction.

They are in src/binding_gate/datasets/deceptive_grounding.py. No benchmark data
(triples or passages) is included in this repository; test fixtures use
invented text.

The upstream NOTICE file reads:

    Deceptive Grounding Benchmark
    Copyright 2026 the Deceptive Grounding authors.

    This release accompanies:
    Cedric Caruzzo, Donggeun Yoo, and Tae Soo Kim.
    Deceptive Grounding: Entity Attribution Failure in Clinical
    Retrieval-Augmented Generation (2026).
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.09349

    The bundled clinical passages are synthetic research stimuli and can contain
    deliberately false or reassigned claims. They are not clinical evidence.

    Citation is requested for scholarly attribution; it does not add a condition
    to the Apache License, Version 2.0.

